Huh?  What're you on?  What's the sys/os2 directory for, if not for OS/2
support, eh?  I've compiled two different versions for OS/2 already.  :-)

BTW, GCC *is* supported for both OS/2 and DOS.  The DOS port of GCC is
called DJGPP, and Nethack sources support this.  The OS/2 port is called
EMX, and the Nethack sources support this (version 0.8f or greater only).

>GCC with a 386/486 is much faster than Microsloth C on the same machines.  Lot
>less disk hits and less delays.  Recommended compile for 386/486 machines.
>(supports up to 4 Meg directly!)

Agreed.  :-)  Although, I couldn't really see much difference with
Nethack under OS/2 (I built both the MSC version (for OS/2 1.x) and the
GCC version (for OS/2 2.0)).  In general, GCC will be faster, but MSC
*does* make code that will run on 8088/286, which GCC won't.

